.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class CELL = Element>
.br
class csmp::PointSource_rhsop< dim, CELL >"Assignment of scalar nodal (Neumann) source or sink terms\&. 

This operator applies (absolute) nodal source terms to the RHS vector as is\&. These values must be precomputed elsewhere\&. One possibility to do this is via the method

.PP
.PP
.nf
NodeCenteredFiniteVolumeTranport::TransformScalarBoundaryValuesIntoNeumannConditions()
.fi
.PP

.PP
It computes gradients normal to the outer model boundary from influxes (sources) assigned and flagged as NEUMANN elsewhere\&. To do this it needs material parameters from the corresponding flow law, for instance the hydraulic conductivity in the case of Darcy's law\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
the nodal term gets applied as many times as the node is a member of an element, i\&.e\&. n\&.Parents() times\&. Therefore the value should be divided by the number of parent elements of the node\&. This is already accounted for by the method \fBGetOperands()\fP\&.

.PP
when applying this term, remember that model must have at least one Dirichlet constraint assigned to make solution unique\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDate\fP
.RS 4
2000 
.RE
.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
Stephan K\&. Matthaei 
.RE
.PP

